     "State-space page methods (common to its figures): signal = Allen-area means (62 areas incl. the ALM / tjM1 ROIs, both hemispheres; image left = ipsilesional) of the adopted hemodynamics-corrected SVD (meegkit_hpfit_lag_refitT, LocaNMF projection), slow drift removed, dF/F x1e3. Trials: engaged trials (engagement gate) with a first lick between the cue and the trial stop (3.5 s if none); first lick = the first camera (LP) lick onset, not the DAQ lick sensor; primary set = contact + incomplete first licks (contact flag = the 3-D first lick matched to the trial). Cohort 1 only (PS92-95), August-only pre (31 sessions), 16 acute / 17 subacute / 43 chronic; 48.6k first-lick trials. Space: per animal, the top 8 PCs of the pre spout x time template (pre sessions other than the ones compared). Stats: change vs the animal's own pre, analysis_kit.boot_delta (paired animals -> sessions, animal-weighted) 95% CI; * = CI excludes 0 (primary); dagger = epoch_change_lmm p < .05 (backup); k/4 = animals above their own pre mean; no correction across readouts or epochs (exploratory). Fig 6.3 · step vs gradual, first-lick-aligned. Top: post-stroke sessions against days on a log axis; thin gray = per-animal fit value = a + b·ln(day), thick = their mean; gray band = pre mean ± SD; panel titles = which of four per-animal time models (step at one day, linear ramp, saturating exponential, log) has the lowest leave-one-session-out error. Bottom: the same readouts against the behavioral recovery axis, far-contra first-cued-lick aim vs the animal’s pre landing (deg, − = ipsilesional; aim_deficit_sessions.csv, the 14.16 axis); lines per animal; gray = pre sessions; titles = within-animal r (PS92 / 93 / 94 / 95) and the p of the within-animal slope (aim circularly shifted over the animal’s day-sorted post-stroke sessions by a random non-zero lag, 2,000 draws). A step model wins in 2 of 24 animal × readout fits; position, the acute-departure axis and the aim itself fall on roughly straight lines in log days — fast early, slower later, no jump. Within animal, the acute-departure axis tracks the aim (r −.78 to −.93, circular shift of session order within animal, 2,000 draws, p < .001) also WITHIN epochs (mixed model with epoch: p .0006); position tracks it (r .55–.90; within epochs p .07). Script: scripts/state_space_step_vs_gradual.py (current main; figure re-rendered 11-16, branch fix/page-figs-1116, tables step_vs_gradual_lick/against_recovery.csv of the replay). File: state_space_recovery/page_figs_nullfix_20261116/ss_step_lick.png (SVD / LocaNMF: ss_step_lick_svd.png, ss_step_lick_lnmfbm.png)",
